Main problem with that is that kelp's pretty scarce until about Medusa 
or some quests: it can only be randomly generated in water and only 
appears in ~10% of pool squares and ~3.33% of moat squares (plenty of 
the latter at Medusa, though).

Also, 'a'pplying a bullwhip down ('>') while levitating or water 
walking can let you get the kelp without going for a swim, but beware 
of drowners--especially couatl, which can't be genocided. Also beware 
of anything with a lightning attack (even if only via items) or a way 
to remove/destroy your armor. Clearing out the monsters on a level 
won't stop new ones from being generated.
